<InfoPage
  title="The 5-Layer Synthesis Engine"
  eyebrow="Editorial & Scientific Standards"
  lede="Our synthesis architecture filters out repetitive media noise, enriches cutting-edge preprints with deep biophysical history, and presents transparent, source-linked intelligence."
>
  <h2>01. Layer 1 — The High-Pass Novelty Gate</h2>
  <p>Most health journalism regurgitates surface-level wellness adages. Our automated Novelty Desk subagent monitors 32 primary scientific feeds (arXiv, bioRxiv, medRxiv, Nature, Wiley, Frontiers) and scores incoming candidates against a strict 58/100 novelty threshold. Candidates that fail to present genuine mechanistic or clinical novelty are automatically discarded.</p>

  <h2>02. Layer 2 — AutoResearch & Deep Context</h2>
  <p>Cutting-edge findings rarely emerge in isolation. For every paper that clears the Novelty Gate, our AutoResearch Subagent traces historical biophysical antecedents—connecting modern preprints to foundational work by scientists like Fritz-Albert Popp (biophotons), Otto Warburg (cellular bioenergetics), and Gerald Pollack (EZ water)—while identifying traditional/ancestral lifestyle parallels backed by physical mechanisms.</p>

  <h2>03. Layer 3 — The 3-Story Daily Triad</h2>
  <p>We respect reader bandwidth. Each edition adheres to a strict 3-story rhythm: one Lead Deep Analysis (8–10 minute read) breaking down complex preprint data, followed by two concise Signals (2-minute reads each) covering actionable cellular, metabolic, or safety intelligence.</p>

  <h2>04. Layer 4 — Evidence Position Badging</h2>
  <p>We replace generic AI hedging with clear, visual scientific maturity badging on every brief:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Established:</strong> Replicated clinical trials & systematic reviews.</li>
    <li><strong>Emerging:</strong> Phase I/II trials, novel animal models, bioRxiv/medRxiv preprints.</li>
    <li><strong>Contested:</strong> Conflicting trial data or competing mechanistic hypotheses.</li>
    <li><strong>Speculative:</strong> Early theoretical biophysics & preliminary arXiv models.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>05. Layer 5 — Direct Source Transparency & Independence</h2>
  <p>Every brief explicitly cites and links to the original DOI or preprint source. Commercial and affiliate relationships never influence story selection, are strictly separated from reporting, and are omitted from our RSS feed. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections & Integrity</h2>
  <p>When a published brief contains a factual error, we update the article and record a timestamped correction note. To flag a concern, contact us through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</InfoPage>
